Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 19:15:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add robotics examples: EU AI Act evidence pack and VLA
 accountability loop

Two runnable examples under examples/ showing how the vouch.robotics
credentials compose end to end for a robot driven by a VLA brain:

- robotics_ai_act_evidence_pack.py: assemble a robot's hardware-rooted
  identity, model provenance, physical capability scope, and tamper-evident
  safety record, run check_conformance for eu-ai-act-high-risk and iso-10218,
  then sign and verify a RobotConformanceAttestation over the report.
- robotics_vla_accountability_loop.py: wrap a VLA brain (e.g. Gemini Robotics
  ER 2) - sign model provenance on load, gate each proposed action against the
  physical capability scope before actuation, and record every decision to a
  tamper-evident encrypted black box.

Index both in examples/README.md. Formatted with black; ruff clean.

